<div class="content-block">
  <div class="section-head">Meeting Summary</div>
  <div class="summary-intro">
    The board opened by announcing it had identified a preferred superintendent candidate and voted unanimously to authorize the chair to enter negotiations, though the candidate's name remained undisclosed. Eighteen Class of 2026 top scholars were recognized in a student-led ceremony, with valedictorian Alexander Davison and salutatorian Audrey LeBleu introducing one another. Finance Director Abigail Kitchen presented the FY2026 year-end budget outlook — projecting a range from a $10,000 surplus to a $2.09 million deficit — alongside an overview of MaineCare billing and a multi-year audit remediation plan. The board approved a consent agenda covering minutes, $23,000+ in donations and scholarships, and personnel contracts, then took first reads on a new agenda policy and an educational equity policy. Public comment raised urgent bus safety concerns about overcrowding during spring track meets, and the board requested a follow-up report at the June meeting.
  </div>
</div>

<div class="content-block">
  <div class="section-head">Transcript Highlights with Timestamps</div>
  <ul class="timeline">

