    <li class="tl-item">
      <div class="tl-time">0:02:00</div>
      <div class="tl-body">
        <div class="tl-topic">Superintendent Search Update</div>
        <div class="tl-desc">Chair reports the board has narrowed the field to two finalists and identified a preferred candidate; the name cannot be disclosed while negotiations are pending.</div>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="tl-item">
      <div class="tl-time">0:02:50</div>
      <div class="tl-body">
        <div class="tl-topic">Vote: Authorize Superintendent Negotiations</div>
        <div class="tl-desc">Board votes unanimously (including both student representatives) to authorize the chair to enter into negotiations with the preferred candidate per executive-session guidance. Moved by Smith, seconded by Feller.</div>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="tl-item">
      <div class="tl-time">0:03:13</div>
      <div class="tl-body">
        <div class="tl-topic">Recognition of Outgoing Student Representatives</div>
        <div class="tl-desc">Board members Feller, Richardson, Holman, and Smith offer extended remarks honoring outgoing student board members Angela Kabisa (three-year member) and valedictorian Alexander Davison. Both students respond with remarks of gratitude.</div>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="tl-item">
      <div class="tl-time">0:14:30</div>
      <div class="tl-body">
        <div class="tl-topic">Top Scholars Recognition Ceremony</div>
        <div class="tl-desc">Superintendent and chair co-present certificates to 18 Class of 2026 top scholars. Valedictorian Alexander Davison and salutatorian Audrey LeBleu introduce one another at the podium.</div>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="tl-item">
      <div class="tl-time">0:36:02</div>
      <div class="tl-body">
        <div class="tl-topic">FY2026–27 Budget Status</div>
        <div class="tl-desc">Finance Director Abigail Kitchen notes the budget has passed city council and heads to a voter referendum on June 9; personnel recall-list notifications are underway.</div>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="tl-item">
      <div class="tl-time">0:36:54</div>
      <div class="tl-body">
        <div class="tl-topic">Elementary Reconfiguration Steering Committee</div>
        <div class="tl-desc">Superintendent announces a 23-member Elementary Reconfiguration Steering Committee has been formed; it is a public committee open for community members to observe.</div>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="tl-item">
      <div class="tl-time">0:39:03</div>
      <div class="tl-body">
        <div class="tl-topic">Enrollment Update</div>
        <div class="tl-desc">Current enrollment stands at 2,776 students. The superintendent notes enrollment dipped early in the year before recovering above the starting count; decline is concentrated at the elementary level, suggesting fewer young families entering the district.</div>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="tl-item">
      <div class="tl-time">0:45:28</div>
      <div class="tl-body">
        <div class="tl-topic">FY2026 Budget Year-End Forecast</div>
        <div class="tl-desc">Finance committee reports 83% of the fiscal year elapsed, 96% of funds expended or encumbered. Updated year-end range: $10,000 surplus to $2.09 million deficit. City council voted to offer up to $2 million in debt forgiveness. The district is also testing payroll encumbrance tracking in the Munis financial system.</div>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="tl-item">
      <div class="tl-time">0:56:02</div>
      <div class="tl-body">
        <div class="tl-topic">MaineCare Billing Overview</div>
        <div class="tl-desc">Director of Instructional Support Kat Cox presents the district's MaineCare billing process (OT, speech, PT — parental consent required, handled through an outside billing agency) and two potential expansions: in-district day treatment and school psychological evaluations, with cautions about audit risk and documentation burden.</div>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="tl-item">
      <div class="tl-time">1:04:35</div>
      <div class="tl-body">
        <div class="tl-topic">Policy Committee Report: First Reads</div>
        <div class="tl-desc">Policy committee chair introduces two first reads: policy BEDB (agenda policy) and a new Educational Equity Policy developed by the DEI director and equity committee.</div>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="tl-item">
      <div class="tl-time">1:09:30</div>
      <div class="tl-body">
        <div class="tl-topic">Consent Agenda Approved</div>
        <div class="tl-desc">Board approves a consent agenda including April meeting minutes, executive session minutes, and donations totaling over $23,000 — including $12,714 from a SPHS graduate for study-abroad scholarships and several named memorial scholarships. Moved by Feller, seconded by Holman. Unanimous.</div>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="tl-item">
      <div class="tl-time">1:19:11</div>
      <div class="tl-body">
        <div class="tl-topic">Public Comment: Bus Safety Concerns</div>
        <div class="tl-desc">Parent Jennifer Christensen describes dangerous overcrowding on buses during spring track meets — 132 athletes packed into buses rated for 71, with students sitting in aisles and on laps on hour-long trips. Transportation employee Jennifer Marshall confirms the issue was reported to administration but not yet resolved.</div>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="tl-item">
      <div class="tl-time">1:25:36</div>
      <div class="tl-body">
        <div class="tl-topic">Superintendent Response to Bus Safety</div>
        <div class="tl-desc">Superintendent acknowledges the specifics were new to him and commits to investigating the following day. Board member Holman requests a status report at the June meeting; the chair agrees.</div>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="tl-item">
      <div class="tl-time">1:28:20</div>
      <div class="tl-body">
        <div class="tl-topic">Kaler Elementary Closure: Student Placements</div>
        <div class="tl-desc">Member Holman requests transparency on how Kaler students will be placed at remaining schools. Principal Mayra Karen explains that minimizing transitions is difficult while the final reconfiguration structure is still undecided; a parent survey on placement preferences was sent that day, with a goal to complete placements by end of May.</div>
      </div>
    </li>

  </ul>
</div>

